Subject: simple IPA: add manual exposure and exposure compensation controls

The software AGC had no controls at all: applications could neither hold an
exposure nor compensate it. Register and implement, following the Adjust
algorithm's pattern:

 - AeEnable (bool, default true): turning it off freezes the current
   exposure and gain.
 - ExposureTime (microseconds) and AnalogueGain: set the exposure and gain
   while AeEnable is off (clamped to the sensor's range).
 - ExposureValue (-2..+2 EV, default 0): exposure compensation while AeEnable
   is on. It moves the mean sample value the AGC aims for by 2^(EV/2), limited
   to what the five-bin histogram can express, so the effect saturates near
   the extremes.

Defaults are unchanged (AE on, EV 0), so applications that set nothing behave
as before. The controls are reset on every configure(), like Adjust's.

